<P STYLE="margin: 0 0 12pt; text-align: justify"></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0 0 12pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">4.16&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
<U>Form D; Blue Sky Filings</U>. The Company agrees to timely file a Form D with respect to the Securities as required under Regulation
D and to provide a copy thereof, promptly upon request of any Purchaser. The Company shall take such action as the Company shall reasonably
determine is necessary in order to obtain an exemption for, or to qualify the Securities for, sale to the Purchasers at the Closing under
applicable securities or &#8220;Blue Sky&#8221; laws of the states of the United States, and shall provide evidence of such actions promptly
upon request of any Purchaser.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0 0 12pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">4.17&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
<U>Additional Investment Right</U>. Subject to the Company&#8217;s receipt of Shareholder Approval, during the period ending eighteen
(18) months following the Effective Date, each Purchaser, pro rata based on such Purchaser&#8217;s initial Subscription Amount relative
to the aggregate initial Subscription Amounts of all Purchasers, shall have the right (the &#8220;<U>Additional Investment Right</U>&#8221;),
but not the obligation, upon notice to the Company from time to time during such period, to purchase up to its pro rata portion of an
aggregate of $91,000,000 of additional shares of Preferred Stock, representing 91,000 additional shares of Preferred Stock, or such lesser
amount as may be available under the Company&#8217;s then-effective authorized preferred stock capitalization and applicable Trading
Market rules, at a purchase price per share equal to the Stated Value (any such shares, the &#8220;<U>Additional Shares</U>&#8221;).&nbsp;
The initial Conversion Price of the first $10,000,000 in the aggregate of the Additional Shares purchased by all Purchasers hereunder
shall be equal to 150% of the Conversion Price of the Conversion Shares and, thereafter, the Additional Shares issuable pursuant to all
subsequent exercises of the Additional Investment Right shall have an initial Conversion Price equal to the lower of (x) the Conversion
Price of the Conversion Shares, and (y) 90% of the arithmetic average of the three (3) lowest VWAPs during the five (5) Trading Days
prior to the date of such Purchaser&#8217;s exercise of the Additional Investment Right, provided that the Conversion Price of the Additional
Shares shall not be less than the Floor Price. The required deliverables for the closing of each purchase pursuant to the Additional
Investment Right shall be the same deliverables set forth in Section 2.2(a)(viii), (ix), (x) and (xii) hereof, and the closing conditions
for each purchase pursuant to the Additional Investment Right shall be the same as the conditions set forth in Section 2.3 hereof, as
applicable to such additional purchase (the date of any such closing, an &#8220;<U>Additional Closing Date</U>&#8221;). The Additional
Investment Right must be exercised with respect to a minimum of $1,000,000 by each participating Purchaser at each Additional Closing.&nbsp;
No Warrants shall be issuable in connection with any exercise of the Additional Investment Right.&nbsp; For the avoidance of doubt, on
each Additional Closing Date, the Company shall file a new certificate of designation setting forth the terms of the Preferred Stock
to be issued as Additional Shares at such Closing, the terms of which shall be substantially similar to the Certificate of Designation,
except that (i) it shall reflect the Conversion Price for such Preferred Stock calculated as required hereunder and (ii) the provisions
set forth in the last two sentences of Section 7(b) of the Certificate of Designation relating to the conversion of shares of Preferred
Stock at the &#8220;Applicable Conversion Price&#8221; shall not apply to any of the Additional Shares, and such language shall not be
included in the applicable certificate of designation for any such Additional Shares. </FONT></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">4.18
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<U>Exercise Procedures</U>. The form of Notice of Exercise included in the Warrants and the
Notice of Conversion included in the Certificate of Designation set forth the totality of the procedures required of the Purchasers in
order to convert the Preferred Stock or exercise the Warrants. No additional legal opinion, other information or instructions shall be
required of the Purchasers to convert their Preferred Stock or exercise their Warrants. Without limiting the preceding sentences, no
ink-original Notice of Conversion or Notice of Exercise shall be required, nor shall any medallion guarantee (or other type of guarantee
or notarization) of any Notice of Conversion or Notice of Exercise form be required in order to convert the Preferred Stock or exercise
the Warrants. The Company shall honor conversions of the Preferred Stock and exercises of the Warrants and shall deliver Underlying Shares
or Warrant Shares in accordance with the terms, conditions and time periods set forth in the Transaction Documents.</FONT></P>

